<title>LUXEMBOURG: EU cuts 1997/98 sugar storage levy.</title>
<headline>EU cuts 1997/98 sugar storage levy.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union will cut the sugar storage levy to 2.0 Ecus per 100 kg in 1997/98 (July/June) from 2.5 Ecus in 1996/97, a European Commission official said.</p>
<p>The decision, taken by the EU's sugar management committee on Wednesday, is based on an expected decision today by EU farm ministers to cut the sugar storage refund to 0.38 Ecus per 100 kg from 0.42 Ecus.  </p>
<p>The Commission official, speaking by phone from Brussels, said the 20 percent cut in the sugar storage levy should result in a 0.8 percent reduction in the sugar support price and follows a cut of about 1.7 percent last year.</p>
<p>&quot;Hopefully this will be passed onto consumers,&quot; the official said.</p>
</text>
